((
Morse trainer
-------------

In order to train my ears for Morse characters and words, I built a
primitive "bug" type of morse key. It has a single blade in the center an
two contact to the sides, one for dits and one for dahs. 

The key then handles timing, in that as long as a contact is closed, it
repeats the symbol associated with that point (dit or dah), at correct
length and proper spacing. 

This also eliminates the issue of "button bounce", both because I will not use
buttons, only bare contact points, so no springs involved, but also because
once detecting a contact on one of the points, it will generate the symbol,
and inter-symbol space following it, which is at least 2 x dit, 
before checking the points again.

I also want to display the characters on an LCD display (I2C), and implement
a simple menu system for setting the speed, all controlled via the morse key.

The input pins for the symbols should be fitted with pulldown resistors,
and the blade should be supplied with VCC.
))


((
The position of the character in the string below, is calcualated as follows: 

- start with 1
- for a dit, left shift one
- for a dah, left shift one and add 1

After playing a sound (dit or dah), we reset timer 0, and in the
main check if more than 3 ticks has elapsed, which indicates 
next letter, and if so show the letter associated with the current code
))

: Chars
	s" __ETIANMSURWDKGOHVF_L_PJBXCYZQ__54_3___2__+____16=/___(_7___8_90____________?________.____@______-___________)_____,"
;

Chars c@ constant Len

: Char (pos -- char) Chars + 1+ c@ ;

(-- pins --)
13 constant LED
6 constant BUZZ  (-- must support PWM --)
7 constant DIT
5 constant DAH

80 constant Tick  (-- length of dit at 20 wpm is 60 ms --)

: In (pin) IN Pins .setIn ;
: Out (pin) IN Pins .setOut ;

: Dr (pin) IN Pins .readDigital ;
: Dw (value pin) IN Pins .writeDigital ;
: Aw (value pin) IN Pins .writeAnalog ;


: Init
	DIT In
	DAH In
	LED Out
	BUZZ Out
;

: On  
	1 LED Dw 
	60 BUZZ Aw ;

: Off 
	0 LED Dw 
	0 BUZZ Dw ;


(-- check if contacts closed --)
: Dit? (--bool) DIT Dr ;
: Dah? (--bool) DAH Dr ;

(-- reset timer 0 --)
: TZero 0 IN Timers .set ;

(-- play dit or dah, followed by a one dit delay before returning --)
: Play (ticks) 
	On Tick * delay 
	Off
	TZero
	(-- enforce at least 1 tick delay --)
	Tick delay ;


(-- get timer 0 millis --)
: CSep? 0 IN Timers .get Tick 3 * > ;

(-- check for symbols (dit/dah), play, and return updated code --)
: Sym (code -- code) 
	Dit? if 
		1 Play
		1 << 
	else
		Dah? if
			3 Play
			1 << 1+
		then
	then
;

(-- look up character from code, show it, return 1 as new code --)
: Show (code -- 1)
	dup 1 == &1 jmp?
	dup Len >= &1 jmp?
	Char emit
	1 ret
	
	/1 drop 1
;
		
(-- Loop forever, and if character separation pause, show character --) 
: Main
	Init
	1 (--current code--)
	/1 
		key? ret?
		Sym                (code)
		CSep? if Show then (code)
		&1 jmp
;

